# IERS TAI-UTC history, as distributed with the receiver firmware.
#
# GPS time was set coincident with UTC at the GPS epoch 1980-01-06,
# at which instant TAI-UTC was 19 s. GPS time has not stepped since.
#
# utc_effective   the UTC instant at which this TAI-UTC value took effect
# tai_utc         TAI minus UTC, whole seconds
# gps_effective   the same step expressed on the GPS time scale; it is
#                 later than utc_effective by the offset that was in
#                 force immediately before the step, because GPS time
#                 does not step when UTC does
# bulletin        issuing IERS bulletin
#
# A lookup MUST compare a UTC argument against utc_effective and a GPS
# argument against gps_effective. The two columns differ by up to 18 s,
# which is exactly the width of the window in which the wrong column
# yields the wrong answer.
#
utc_effective          tai_utc  gps_effective          bulletin
1980-01-01T00:00:00    19       1980-01-01T00:00:00    IERS Bulletin C -- GPS epoch reference
1981-07-01T00:00:00    20       1981-07-01T00:00:00    Bulletin C 1
1982-07-01T00:00:00    21       1982-07-01T00:00:01    Bulletin C 2
1983-07-01T00:00:00    22       1983-07-01T00:00:02    Bulletin C 3
1985-07-01T00:00:00    23       1985-07-01T00:00:03    Bulletin C 5
1988-01-01T00:00:00    24       1988-01-01T00:00:04    Bulletin C 8
